Z||000010||MR2KLR||12-15-2001||11:09 PM||||Abut a year ago I raced a brand new, window sticker, temp tag & all 2000 Eclipse GT (V6 5-speed) Stop light to stop light for abou an hour about 2 O'clock in the morning on a saturday night  in my 1995 Nissan etended cab pickup (V6 5-speed and it was good door to door racing. about a week affter that Me (in my truck) and a friend (88 Fiero GT Auto) both went to the track for the first times in our cars and I steadly beat him by much more than 3 car lenghts my times where 14.9-15.6 while hes best ET was 15.9 and he even had a fiero store head pipe altough he did hav 100k miles on the car but either way I don't realy think you have a shot at beating him although the one I raced was a 5-speed so it may be faster and you have a 5-speed while my friend has a Auto. good racing to ya  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <BR>Black 88 Coupe: 120 MPH spedo, Aux. gauge pod, 195/55VR14 Potenza RE-71 tires, GT exhaust & ground F/X Soon to have 16" White Beretta GTZ W/ 215/45ZR16's<BR><A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
