Z||000012||Oreif||12-16-2001||10:21 AM||||Against an Eclipse GT, a stick Fiero should be even or slightly ahead. The Eclipse has a 200hp 24-valve V-6 and is close to 3100 lbs in weight. So with the loss of HP thru the auto trans and more weight it would be close.<BR>The engine/trans in the Eclipse is the same as in my Galant ES-V6. The auto trans isn't the best for racing. I know the auto trans has some issues that would give a stick Fiero an advantage.<BR>A stick Eclipse would win given both drivers are of equal shifting skill.<P>As for Z24's, The 80's Z24's had a 2.8L V-6 with 125HP. A Fiero is faster since they have more HP and less weight (weight difference is only about 150lbs) In 1989 they started using 3.1L engines with 150HP. An auto Z24 would still lose to a stick Fiero. In 1991 they were using the 4-spd auto's which had better gearing. An auto Z24 w/4-spd auto would do better but I think with a decent driver the Fiero would still win slightly. The Fiero would be way better off the line and once the Fiero was ahead, the Z24 would be close but doubt it could pass the Fiero. Adding stick's to the Z24's the above results would be different. The 3.1L engines had more HP and torque so the stick Z24's would win.<BR>The new Z24's are a huge disappointment. The 150HP 4-cyl doesn't have the torque to get the car moving right away So the auto or stick cars are both dogs. They should have went with the 3.4L for the Z24's they would be screamers!<P>The above is factory stock. I know a few who did things to make the Z24's faster. On the 80's just changing the top intake an throttle body to a Fiero was a big improvement. (Fiero TB is 52MM the original Z24's had 48MM) The 3.1L Z24's had more HP and torque and with some minor modding could be screamers. If I remember the trick was to open the exhaust and use a Grand Prix intake/TB. The 7MM difference in TB's was a world of difference on the 3.1L.<P><BR>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">            <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||87gt guy||12-16-2001||01:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stingant0:<BR><B>You WILL get embarassed....heck I got beat by an automatic z24 with only a k&N. I had headers, no cat, UD pulley, and K&N. And Im an awsome shifter. I beat him to 60 though, so my car is about 0-60 7.9. <P>PS..DO NOT race a Prevea...yes the mid engine minivan you WILL GET VERY EMBARSSED. Trust me!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Man...  No offense but I don't think you know how to drive it to the max, I know. I smoked a 3.1 z-24 when I banged it into 3rd. I also smoked a lexus gs 300, the big new ones, passed him while in second, went up to about 6500rpm, and banged 3rd, he was getting further and further in my mirror. I can understand how I won because those cars are big and heavy, but I know the eclipse is lighter. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||stingant0||12-16-2001||02:11 PM||||Well I know how to drive VERY well...i autocross and drag at the track. I have the video. I had him off the line and when I went into 3rd he passed me. He runs 16.01 at the track. I know my car was running lean. His car was a 96 z24. The race really shocked me I thought I would kill him.. well I guess I have to give you guys the video..I raced a 96 Avenger also I killed it!!||||reg||1
