Z||000022||LoW_KeY||12-17-2001||10:41 PM||||Hmm all and all its how you drive and how your car acts.. I have a killer car and not afraid to attack the V8 class of cars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>My moms got a 94 grand-am quad and my dads like lets race then laughs from a dead stop I can make that car a little spec in my mirror as my dad saw right before I put it in storage.  I would think you could take the quad, but like I said it matters if your cars been kept up runs strong.. yada, yada, yada.<P>Go and find out thats all I have to say.. I have and I have lost a few times, last race I lost was to a 95-96 V8 Camaro, not sure if I really lost that one or not, because the guy wasn't even gaining on me until I backed off at 100. Not to mention my car was shaking like there was no tomorrow (damn alignments) or I would've kept going.<P>Just be safe if you do it, I just can't wait till I bust it out and do a full performance rebuild  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>All and all I can say I got some confidence in my car from racing a modded LT-1 93 camaro, mustangs and such and such, the guy with the LT-1 told my friend "jesus you guys had the 4 banger really hauling."<P>-KC||||reg||1
